content.text:
Now, check whether `Service` model relation `revenueAccount` and `discountAccount` works with eager load; yes.

Potential issue: `Product::with(...)->lockForUpdate()` — Eloquent `lockForUpdate` with eager load runs two queries; the lock applies to product query, fine.

Now let's write the regression test file. I need to be careful with imports and helpers.

Test class setup:
```php
namespace Tests\Feature;

use App\Actions\Accounting\PostDoubleEntryJournalAction;
use App\Actions\Piket\ClosePosShiftAction;
use App\Actions\Piket\OpenPosShiftAction;
use App\Actions\Pos\CheckoutPosTransactionAction;
use App\Actions\Pos\VoidPosTransactionAction;
use App\DTOs\Accounting\JournalEntryData;
use App\DTOs\Accounting\JournalLineData;
use App\DTOs\Piket\ShiftOpeningData;
use App\DTOs\Piket\StudentAttendanceSlotData;
use App\DTOs\Pos\CartItemData;
use App\DTOs\Pos\CheckoutPayloadData;
use App\Enums\AbsenceStatus;
use App\Enums\JournalType;
use App\Enums\PaymentMethod;
use App\Models\AccountingPeriod;
use App\Models\CashBookEntry;
use App\Models\ChartOfAccount;
use App\Models\JournalEntry;
use App\Models\PiketSchedule;
use App\Models\PosShift;
use App\Models\Product;
use App\Models\Service;
use App\Models\User;
use App\Services\Accounting\FinancialStatementGenerator;
use Illuminate\Foundation\Testing\RefreshDatabase;
use Illuminate\Support\Carbon;
use Tests\TestCase;
```

Properties: teacher, students array, admin, student.

setUp: seed; assign. Ensure current accounting period exists (seeder does). Maybe `AccountingPeriod::where('is_closed', false)->firstOrFail()`.

Helper `openShift(string $openingCash = '200000.0000'): PosShift` opens with teacher as opener and 3 distinct students.

Helper `retailProduct(): Product` update stock/price/cost.

Helper `checkout(PosShift $shift, array $items, PaymentMethod $method, string $amountPaid, string $manualDiscount = '0.0000'): PosTransaction` using student as cashier.

Need `use App\Models\PosTransaction;`.

Test 1: authorization boundaries.
```php
public function test_students_cannot_access_staff_transactions_or_shift_mutations(): void
{
    $this->actingAs($this->student)->get('/transactions')->assertForbidden();
    $this->actingAs($this->student)->post('/shift/open', [])->assertForbidden();
    $this->actingAs($this->student)->post('/shift/close', [])->assertForbidden();
    $this->actingAs($this->student)->post('/transactions/1/void', [])->assertForbidden();

    $response = $this->actingAs($this->student)->get('/shift');
    $response->assertOk();
    $response->assertSee('Shift belum dibuka');
    $response->assertDontSee('Isi kas awal dan status kehadiran 3 petugas piket.');
}
```
Wait: `/transactions/1/void` route has middleware staff; even if id doesn't exist, middleware runs before controller, returns 403. Good. But route model? route defined as `Route::post('/transactions/{id}/void', ...)`; middleware group applies. Good.

Does `/shift` GET show "Shift belum dibuka" twice? It appears in page header and card. Fine. `assertDontSee('Isi kas awal...')` ensures open form hidden. Also "Tutup shift" hidden.

Test 2: duplicate open shift:
```php
public function test_only_one_pos_shift_can_be_open_at_a_time(): void
{
    $shift = $this->openShift();
    $this->expectException(\DomainException::class);
    $this->expectExceptionMessage('Masih ada shift kasir yang terbuka');
    $this->openShift('100000.0000');
}
```
But after exception, we might want assert count; can't after expectException. Use try/catch:
```php
try { $this->openShift('100000.0000'); $this->fail(...); } catch (\DomainException $e) { $this->assertStringContainsString(...); }
$this->assertSame(1, PosShift::where('status','OPEN')->count());
```
Also test controller duplicate returns session error:
```php
$response = $this->actingAs($this->teacher)->post('/shift/open', [...]);
$response->assertSessionHasErrors('shift');
```
But the controller validates supervisor PIN etc. We can use valid payload. However, `OpenPosShiftAction` will throw; controller catches and adds error. We can add this to same test after action attempt? The first shift is open. Build payload with teacher pin 123456, opening 100000, slots 1-3 with distinct students, status PRESENT. Post; assert session errors 'shift' with message. This tests controller path. But the action-level test already confirms. Could do both in one test.

Payload:
```php
'supervisor_teacher_id' => $this->teacher->id,
'supervisor_pin' => '123456',
'opening_cash_balance' => '100000',
'slots' => [
  ['scheduled_user_id' => $this->students[0]->id, 'status' => 'PRESENT'],
  ...
]
```
Validation requires `slots` size 3 and distinct. `absence_reason` nullable, `substituted_user_id` nullable. Good.
Then assert session has errors `shift` containing 'Masih ada shift kasir yang terbuka'. `assertSessionHasErrors(['shift' => 'Masih ada shift kasir yang terbuka'])` checks exact? Laravel `assertSessionHasErrors` with array values checks message contains? It checks exact string? Let me recall: `assertSessionHasErrors(array $keys, $format = null, $errorBag = 'default')` — if keys have values, it asserts the error messages contain the value? In Laravel, `assertSessionHasErrors(['field' => 'message'])` checks that the session errors contain the key and that the message matches exactly? Looking at `Session::assertHasErrors`: if is_array($keys), it checks `$errors->has($key)` and if value not null, `$errors->first($key) === $value`. I think exact. Use `assertSessionHasErrors('shift')` then `$this->assertStringContainsString('Masih ada shift', session('errors')->first('shift'))`.

Test 3: QRIS expected cash:
```php
$shift = $this->openShift();
$product = $this->makeRetailProduct('10000.0000','6000.0000','10.0000');
$tx = $this->checkout($shift, [new CartItemData('RETAIL_PRODUCT', (string)$product->id, null, '1.0000','0.0000')], PaymentMethod::QRIS, '10000.0000');
$this->assertSame('10000.0000', (string)$tx->grand_total);
$closed = app(ClosePosShiftAction::class)->execute((string)$shift->id, '200000.0000', (string)$this->teacher->id);
$this->assertSame('200000.0000', (string)$closed->system_expected_cash);
$this->assertSame('0.0000', (string)$closed->cash_discrepancy);
$this->assertFalse(JournalEntry::where('journal_type', JournalType::CASH_DISCREPANCY->value)->exists());
```
But wait: opening cash 200000, QRIS sale doesn't affect 1-1101. Close expected 200000. Good.
Also assert `CashBookEntry` for QRIS exists with account 1-1103 and no 1-1101 entry with shift id? The journal posts QRIS debit to 1-1103, so BKU has entry on 1-1103. Assert `CashBookEntry::where('pos_shift_id',$shift->id)->whereHas('cashAccount', fn($q)=>$q->where('account_code','1-1101'))->doesntExist()`. This directly verifies exclusion. Good.
But note: close shift posts no journal when discrepancy zero. Good.
Potential issue: `ClosePosShiftAction` actual closing cash string '200000.0000'; `StrictCurrency` not involved. Fine.
`$closed->cash_discrepancy` cast? PosShift casts `cash_discrepancy` maybe decimal:4; check. It likely does. If null? It updates. Good.

Test 4: BKU backdated ordering:
Need create journals. Use a helper `postCashJournal(string $date, string $amount, string $number, string $description): JournalEntry`. Account codes: debit 1-1101, credit 4-9101. Use `Carbon::parse($date)`. Journal type `JournalType::CASH_IN`? Check enum values. Let's inspect JournalType.

